## 3. `useWelcomeHint` Hook (Full Content)

**File:** `C:\Users\zemuro\Antigravity\kimi_extension_mod\webview-ui\src\hooks\useWelcomeHint.tsx` (131 lines)

```tsx
export function useWelcomeHint(): WelcomeHint {
  const [hasAgentMd, setHasAgentMd] = useState<boolean | null>(null);
  const [hasHistory, setHasHistory] = useState<boolean | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    bridge.checkFileExists("AGENT.md").then(setHasAgentMd).catch(() => setHasAgentMd(false));
    bridge.getConsiliumSessions().then((s) => setHasHistory(s.length > 0)).catch(() => setHasHistory(false));
  }, []);

  return useMemo(() => {
    // First time user: show shortcut guide
    if (hasHistory === false) {
      return HINT_FIRST_TIME;
    }
    // 30% chance to show AGENT.md hint if missing
    if (hasAgentMd === false && withProbability(0.3)) {
      return HINT_AGENT_MD;
    }
    return pickRandom(HINTS_POOL);
  }, [hasAgentMd, hasHistory]);
}
```

**Key logic:**
1. Checks if `AGENT.md` exists in the workspace root (via `bridge.checkFileExists("AGENT.md")`)
2. Checks if there are any existing Consilium sessions (via `bridge.getConsiliumSessions()`)
3. **First time (no history):** Shows a keyboard shortcut guide
4. **AGENT.md missing (30% chance):** Shows "Let me map your codebase - Run /init to scan the project"
5. **Otherwise:** Random tip from a pool of 8 hints

**CRITICAL:** The hook checks for `AGENT.md` (capital A, no S), **not** `AGENTS.md`. This is likely a bug — the CLI uses `AGENTS.md` (with an S).

